The local `sigorbit-c8-257-v1` checkpoint was used during pre-release
engineering so extraction and parity could be tested, but it is excluded from
Git and source/binary distributions. A 2026-08-07 pixel audit
identified the training aggregate as genuine CEDAR and BHSig260 samples. CEDAR
has no explicit licence grant; BHSig260 is stated only to be available “for
research purposes”. This notice intentionally
does not grant permission to redistribute the checkpoint. Do not publish it
until upstream permission or counsel approval is recorded. No training images
are included. See docs/DATASET_LICENSE_AUDIT.md.

